    description: "Typed stable ids: a qualified type inside a compound type is hashed as written, so (java.lang.String) -> Unit and (String) -> Unit hash apart.\n\nSpelling sensitivity, not a collapse: the same declaration written with a qualified or an imported name gets a different typed id. Same choice the C# tuple and Dart function-type rules made in PR #2276. REPRO and context: /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr3/tojov/RESULTS.md residual 4 (PR 3 commit 4e0163454). Not measured on real trees."  # 2f91
